<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">purgāmen</span></b> , ĭnis,
			n.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>What was annually swept</i> or <i>washed from the temple of Vesta</i>, i. e. <i>the
				dirt</i> or <i>filth swept out</i>, <i>the sweepings</i>, <i>offscourings</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 6, 713</span></i> and 227; v.
			stercus.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A means of purgation</i>, <i>purification</i>, or <i>expiation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caedis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 11, 409</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mali,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					2, 35</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 23</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					M. 15, 327</span></i>
			: aquae, i. e. <i>baptism</i>, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 6, 30.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Purity</i>, <i>clearness</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 7, 80</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
